note The node font's cell at the current zoom and the pixel padding inside a node. Layout happens in cells and rows; this turns it into pixels, so zooming scales positions by the factor the text really grew by, not by the nominal zoom. The spacing constants are in the same units: GAP_X is cells between columns, GAP_Y rows between stacked subtrees.

